2026-11-14 11:24:22,088 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] ### Case Q1: Anti-Virus Check Results
2026-11-14 11:24:22,088 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **Answer**: No viruses were detected on the Dell Latitude CPi system. Comprehensive forensic analysis revealed zero results for antivirus software installation or virus/malware signatures. The system operated as an unprotected attack platform rather than as a compromised victim system.
2026-11-14 11:24:22,089 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] ### Key Findings
2026-11-14 11:24:22,089 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] 1. **Network Sniffing Infrastructure**: The system contained Ethereal, Cain & Abel, and WinPcap driver, with an actual TCPDUMP packet capture file recovered containing HTTP/1 traffic from 192.168.254.2.
2026-11-14 11:24:22,090 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] 2. **Suspicious User Account**: A "Mr. Evil" account with IRC participation in hacker-oriented channels (#Elite.Hackers, #ISO-WAREZ, #evilfork) documented between August 20-25, 2004.
2026-11-14 11:24:22,090 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] 3. **Organized Hacking Tool Collection**: Directory structure containing compressed archives of exploitation tools (Pwdump, enum, Nmap NT) organized following attack chain methodology.
2026-11-14 11:24:22,091 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] 4. **No Attribution to Greg Schardt**: Comprehensive search returned zero references to "Greg Schardt" in any evidence source, preventing definitive attribution to the named suspect.
2026-11-14 11:24:22,091 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] 5. **Operational Timeline**: Active configuration and deployment August 19-27, 2004, with evidence suggesting 3-4 weeks of field operation targeting wireless access point users.
2026-11-14 11:24:22,092 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] ### Incident Assessment
2026-11-14 11:24:22,093 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] The Dell CPi represents a purpose-built wireless network interception platform designed to capture unencrypted credentials at public hotspots (Starbucks, T-Mobile). The system exhibits moderate technical sophistication and demonstrates clear criminal intent toward credential harvesting and financial fraud.
2026-11-14 11:24:22,094 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **Scope**: Potentially hundreds of wireless users exposed during deployment period
2026-11-14 11:24:22,094 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **Impact**: Credential compromise, identity theft risk, financial account exposure
2026-11-14 11:24:22,095 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **Attribution**: Unknown perpetrator operating under "Mr. Evil" nickname; cannot confirm link to Greg Schardt
